Great question. DAG dependencies in DAG Factory work at two levels — **within a DAG** (task dependencies) and **across DAGs** (DAG dependencies). Let me cover all options.

---

## Level 1 — Task Dependencies Within a DAG

This is straightforward in DAG Factory YAML using the `dependencies` field.

```yaml
cash_management__payments__ingestion__daily:
  schedule: "0 6 * * *"

  tasks:
    extract_raw:
      operator: plugins.operators.gcs_sql_bigquery_operator.GCSSqlToBigQueryOperator
      query_gcs_path: "gs://bucket/sql/extract_raw.sql"
      default_dataset_key: "cash_mgmt"
      destination_dataset_key: "raw"
      destination_table_id: "payments_raw"
      # No dependencies — this runs first

    transform_curated:
      operator: plugins.operators.gcs_sql_bigquery_operator.GCSSqlToBigQueryOperator
      query_gcs_path: "gs://bucket/sql/transform_curated.sql"
      default_dataset_key: "cash_mgmt"
      destination_dataset_key: "curated"
      destination_table_id: "payments_curated"
      dependencies: [extract_raw]              # runs after extract_raw

    load_reporting:
      operator: plugins.operators.gcs_sql_bigquery_operator.GCSSqlToBigQueryOperator
      query_gcs_path: "gs://bucket/sql/load_reporting.sql"
      default_dataset_key: "cash_mgmt"
      destination_dataset_key: "reporting"
      destination_table_id: "payments_report"
      dependencies: [transform_curated]        # runs after transform_curated

    send_notification:
      operator: airflow.operators.email.EmailOperator
      to: ["cash-mgmt@company.com"]
      subject: "Payments ingestion complete"
      html_content: "Daily payments pipeline finished successfully."
      dependencies: [load_reporting]           # runs last
```

This produces:
```
extract_raw → transform_curated → load_reporting → send_notification
```

### Fan-out and Fan-in also supported

```yaml
  tasks:
    start:
      operator: airflow.operators.dummy.DummyOperator

    payments_load:
      operator: ...
      dependencies: [start]

    settlements_load:
      operator: ...
      dependencies: [start]        # fan-out — both run in parallel after start

    reconciliation:
      operator: ...
      dependencies: [payments_load, settlements_load]   # fan-in — waits for both
```

